From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:05:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: browse panorama prefetch reads cover headers
 ahead of the viewport
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The browse grid prefetched every loaded row by decoding a 128 px hardware
bitmap, with the memory cache off, then threw the bitmap away. Those
requests shared Coil's 3 decoder slots with the covers on screen, so the
visible cells decoded again from disk. The queue started over at index 0
on every paging append and never cancelled rows that had scrolled away.
While those new covers loaded, frames dropped to 53-62% of animation ticks,
and each newly learnt tall cover could still force a 16-20 ms structural
relayout if it committed mid-fling.

The default arm now asks Coil only to fetch the file, then a request
decoder reads the header with inJustDecodeBounds and returns a 1x1
ColorImage. Coil runs that factory before the loader's decoders, and the
request uses Dispatchers.IO, so it does not take a decoder slot or a
hardware bitmap. A header BitmapFactory cannot read is left unknown.

Only the rows from the first visible cell through two viewports ahead are
queued, two at a time. Enqueueing pauses while any panorama grid is
scrolling and resumes when it settles. A request more than one window
behind is cancelled. Finished ids are remembered, so a new page does not
restart at 0.

DECODE keeps the old 128 px path. OFF prefetches nothing. The mode is
read in composition.

Grid covers honor the crossfade and hardware toggles. Both defaults still
pass the MangaCover model through unchanged, so the memory-cache key and
CoverRequestInterceptor see the same data.

